    {
      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
      "Text": "The development of frost and heat damage functions was supported by the ‘Frost and Heat Management Analytics’ (FAHMA) project via funding from the Grains Research and Development Corporation (GRDC; Grant No. CSP2204-009RTX).",
      "Name": "Funding Acknowledgement",
      "ResourceName": null,
      "Children": [],
      "Enabled": true,
      "ReadOnly": false
    },
    {
      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
      "Text": "Data description: Please refer to https://doi.org/10.25919/endv-q229.\n\nDisclaimer: This dataset is provided “as is” without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to its accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular purpose. The creators and contributors shall not be liable for any damages arising from its use. \n\nLicense: This dataset is released under [Creative Commons Attribution Noncommercial-Share Alike 4.0 Licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/) in [CSIRO DAP](https://doi.org/10.25919/endv-q229).\n \nFor further inquiries or permission requests, please contact Dr Lindsay Bell (Lindsay.Bell@csiro.au).\n\n\nWhen citing this dataset, please use the following reference: Bell, L., Lawrence, D., Baird, J., Erbacher, A., Aisthorpe, D., Parkinson, E., Brooke, G.,  Hertel, K., Gentry, J., McMullen, G., Simpfendorfer, S., Whish, J., Ruttledge, A., 2024. Northern farming systems data. https://doi.org/10.25919/endv-q229.\n \n \nWhen using the damage functions, please use the following reference for more information: Hu, P., He, D., Zheng, B., Whish, J., Kirkegaard, J., Bell, L., Leske, B., Chen, S., Uppal, R., Biddulph, B., Trethowan, R., Beletse, Y., Lilley, J., 2026. Event-based frost and heat damage functions improve yield predictions of APSIM canola and wheat: formulation, calibration, and evaluation. Agricultural and Forest Meteorology 386, 111239. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agrformet.2026.111239",
      "Name": "Data Ownership Acknowledgement",
      "ResourceName": null,
      "Children": [],
      "Enabled": true,
      "ReadOnly": false
    },
